Selection Sort:
Selection Sort finds the minimum element from the unsorted portion and places it at the correct position.

Case          Time Complexity
Best Case        	O(n²)
Average Case	    O(n²)
Worst Case	      O(n²)
Space Complexity	  O(1)

Selection Sort always performs comparisons, even if the array is already sorted.
Therefore, its best, average, and worst cases are all O(n²).
It uses only a small amount of extra memory.
